Timing and focus for the SDL3 host. On Windows the vertical blanks are paced by timed waits, which are only as fine as the system timer: the host now asks for 1 ms (raylib did, SDL3 does not) and opts out of power throttling, including Windows 11's rule that drops a process's timer requests while its window is covered, minimized or out of sight, so the game keeps its full speed in the background (PS2X_POWER_THROTTLING=1 keeps Windows' default). PS2X_WINDOW_FOCUS=1 lets a placed window (test runs) take the focus and raises it, where it otherwise opens without taking it.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_sdl.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_sdl.cpp
